he scope planned by the policy."],[1494,"This mode requires the `jitp_config.provisioning_role_arn` field to be configured with the ARN of an IAM role AWS IoT Core can assume to execute the template. If not configured, the connector uses the default `arn:aws:iam::{account}:role/JITPRole` and logs a warning. The administrator must ensure that role exists in the account and has the necessary permissions before enabling JITP mode."],[551,"This model lets you represent people, identity-provider groups, service accounts and devices without coupling authorization to a specific provider."],[2720,"This page is organized in four parts. Read them in order before you upgrade production:"],[1715,"This path is intended for those starting to administer device identities. You will register `device-001` and assign an existing certificate to check the relationship between device, DMS and identity history."],[2590,"This path is intended for those starting to administer PKI or needing a first X.509 client identity. It ends with three files: a root CA certificate, an end-entity certificate and the client's private key."],[560,"This path protects APIs that join the platform through the Gateway but do not natively implement Lamassu's authorization SDK. Job Manager is the current example. The same pattern allows integrating other HTTP services as long as their routes are described in an `authz` HTTP schema."],[2673,"This policy covers the source code, configuration, and CI/CD workflows of the lamassuiot, lamassu-dashboard, and lamassu-helm repositories."],[1975,"This preserves SAN, but does not establish that the requester is entitled to those DNS names, IP addresses, emails or URIs. Validate that authorization before issuing. OCSP and CRL locations come from the issuance service configuration; `Honor Extensions` does not copy CSR distribution points."],[1828,"This procedure is for the PKI operator replacing an authority in use. You need access to CAs, keys and profiles, a dependency inventory and coordination with trust-store and device owners. Before switching issuance, prepare a test cohort and decide the criterion for ending overlap."],[280,"This requests `192.168.1.50`; it does not claim the IP on your LAN or make it reachable."],[319,"This requires distinct SNI hostnames and cluster networking outside the Lamassu chart."],[1610,"This section connects PKI rules to the device client. Preparation follows this order:"],[2158,"This separation makes it possible to migrate a fleet: you temporarily accept certificates from the old hierarchy, issue with the new one and distribute both chains during the overlap."],[2388,"This tab checks whether a signature corresponds to the associated public key."],[2381,"This tab uses the private key to generate a digital signature over a message or an already computed *digest*."],[316,"Three independent `LoadBalancer` Services cannot all reserve the same node ports 80 and 443 through K3s ServiceLB. Use one shared Gateway, allocate distinct VIPs with another load-balancer implementation, or use different ports."],[1279,"Three trust relationships"],[2200,"Time from `thisUpdate` to `nextUpdate`."],[2203,"Time since the issuance of the latest published CRL that triggers scheduled renewal; `0` disables only this trigger. The effective granularity is bounded by the job frequency (see Periodic and automatic regeneration)."],[1266,"Timeout or error after issuance"],[1212,"Timeout, HTTP 500 or installation failure"],[373,"TLS"],[87,"TLS behavior"],[204,"TLS with an existing Secret"],[1890,"To administer CAs, you need authority and key permissions, a reachable engine and a reviewed profile. An external consumer does not trust a CA merely because it appears in this inventory: agree root and chain distribution separately."],[2956,"To apply migrations by hand, `goose-lamassu` must run against the `pki` database with `search_path=<schema>` in the connection string. The binary validates only `search_path`, not the database name, so check `dbname=pki` before running it, and repeat for `kms`, `ca`, `va`, `devicemanager`, `dmsmanager` and `alerts`:"],[1338,"To avoid infinite loops, the connector ignores any event whose CloudEvent `source` field matches its own origin URI. This prevents the metadata writes the connector itself performs from re-triggering the same flow."],[2455,"To check a change, save an earlier response, revoke a test certificate and request another response. The new query should reflect persisted status; compare timestamps to rule out reuse of an earlier response. If it fails, follow PKI troubleshooting."],[1889,"To design a full chain or replace an authority in production, see CA hierarchy and rotation. If you need to standardize what each authority can sign, use Certificate profiles."],[242,"To install a local checkout instead:"],[2610,"To manage a device identity in Lamassu, follow Manual registration. That path includes DMS preparation."],[2609,"To operate certificates, continue with Certificates and Validation."],[667,"To revoke access immediately, disable the principal or revoke its grants. Disabling a principal keeps its configuration and associations for investigation or restoration, but it stops taking part in matching."],[1597,"To start with an existing certificate, use Register a device manually. You can then prepare enrollment and renewal for the next device."],[1756,"To use the identity in AWS IoT Core, also prepare trust and permissions in the destination. Check the connection from the device after installing the required key, certificate and chain."],[1461,"Transition"],[1496,"Transition"],[1510,"Transition"],[1539,"Transition"],[1332,"Troubleshooting"],[2716,"Troubleshooting"],[937,"Trust distribution"],[1277,"Trust distribution and updates"],[2131,"Trust model"],[1629,"Trusted issuers, validation and device permissions in the destination."],[2627,"Try **Sign / Verify** in KMS; check provider permissions and availability."],[519,"Two decision systems"],[2849,"Tw